{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from nonblack-brigandish-guillemot: its closing plan review raised this as an advisory finding. After ADR 0125, rebar checks op-certs for validity only unless the verifying environment lists the keys it trusts in `verify.trusted_opcert_keys`. ADR 0125 says that list belongs to each environment's own configuration, not the repository.\n\nNothing enforces that. `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` is an ordinary `[verify]` key (`src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, `VerifyConfig.trusted_opcert_keys`). The CI op-cert gate is the `verify-opcert` step of `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`, which runs `rebar verify-opcert` on the checked-out change. `cli()` in `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py` calls `config.compose_config(root=args.root)` and `trusted_opcert_pairs(args.root)` (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:114`), and both resolve the project layer through `_discover_project_config` (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:160`), which reads the working-tree `rebar.toml`. So a change under review that adds its own key to `rebar.toml`, drops `verify.require_environment`, or sets `[tracker] dir` to an empty directory (the gate also resolves its store through `config.tracker_dir(args.root)`, `verify_opcert.py:138`, and through `show_ticket`/`current_material_fingerprint`) loosens the very gate run that checks it. Reproduced locally: a change listing its own key and closing a ticket under a certificate signed by that key passes `rebar verify-opcert --require-environment <env>` with exit 0.\n\n## Approach (operator decision, 2026-11-20)\n\nThe gate resolves its trust configuration from main's committed `rebar.toml`, never from the `rebar.toml` in the change under review. A change can edit `rebar.toml` freely, but the edit only takes effect for gating after it has itself merged through review.\n\nImplement this in-process in `rebar verify-opcert`, so it holds under any CI provider or none:\n\n- New module `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` with `gate_config(root) -> (Config, source, OperationSnapshot)`. It composes the same labelled layers as `load_config` (`src/rebar/config.py:468` `_compose`) — user config, project, env overrides, process `-c` overrides — but the project layer is the project config committed at the base ref, read with `git show <ref>:<path>`. It walks from the project root up to the git top level and takes the nearest `rebar.toml`, else a `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.rebar]`. It does not reuse `_discover_project_config` (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:160`) because that reads files on disk and honours a `$REBAR_CONFIG` pointer; the gate ignores `$REBAR_CONFIG`, since a pointer could name a working-tree file. The working-tree project config is never read.\n- Base ref: `refs/remotes/origin/main` only, the ref attested gates already treat as reviewed main (`rebar.llm.gate_source.DEFAULT_REF`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:71`). Failure handling, every arm:\n  - a remote exists but `origin/main` does not resolve: `ConfigError`, exit 2, naming the `git fetch` that fixes it (falling back to the working tree there would reopen the hole);\n  - the ref resolves but `git show` of a present path fails (for example a blobless clone cannot fetch the blob) or the TOML does not parse: `ConfigError`, exit 2;\n  - the path is absent at the ref (`git cat-file -e` fails, which needs only trees): fall through to the next candidate, then to an empty project layer;\n  - no remote at all (`git remote` prints nothing): no reviewed branch and no change under review, so the working-tree configuration is kept (local-only projects and the existing remote-less fixtures in `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py`).\n- The same configuration is returned as an `OperationSnapshot` (`src/rebar/_operation_config.py:81`). `cli()` binds it with `bind_operation_snapshot` for the whole run, so `config.tracker_dir` (`src/rebar/config.py:152`, which reads a bound snapshot's `tracker.dir` after the environment override) and every nested config read use main's values. `cli()` takes `require_environment`, `opcert_enforce_since` and `trusted_opcert_keys` from it and prints the source to stderr. `trusted_opcert_pairs` is split so the gate can parse a list it already holds (`opcert_pairs(entries)`). The body moves into a `_gate(args, cfg)` helper so `cli` stays under the complexity ceiling.\n- `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`: the `verify-opcert` step fetches `refs/heads/main` into `refs/remotes/origin/main` (blobless, after the pack measurement) before running the gate.\n- Docs: the `verify-opcert` parser description (regenerated `src/rebar/_cli/help/*.txt` and `docs/cli-reference.md`), `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md` (the new exit-2 cases), and `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` (an enforcement flip takes effect after it merges, not in its own gate run).\n\nOut of scope, stated so the boundary is explicit: the environment layer stays (ADR 0125 puts the trust list in the verifying environment), and keeping that layer, the gate's own code and the workflow file out of the change's reach belongs to the CI lane, not to this fix. The sibling `verify-identity` gate reads `identity.*` from the working tree the same way; that is a separate gate and is not changed here.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added: the base ref is fixed at `origin/main`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt`, `docs/cli-reference.md`\n- `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n`tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, using a local bare repo as `origin`:\n\n- The attack, end to end: main's committed `rebar.toml` trusts key A; a change branch commits a `rebar.toml` that also lists key B and closes a ticket under a B-signed completion certificate. `rebar verify-opcert --require-environment <env>` exits 1 with `untrusted`, and stderr names the base-branch `rebar.toml` as the trust source. After the change is pushed to `origin/main` and fetched, the same command exits 0. This test fails (exit 0) against the old gate.\n- A dirty working-tree `rebar.toml` and the change's committed one are both ignored; the trust list equals main's.\n- A change cannot drop main's `require_environment`.\n- The environment's `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS` still applies (ADR 0125's home for the list).\n- `pyproject.toml` `[tool.rebar]` on main is used when main has no `rebar.toml`.\n- A change setting `[tracker] dir` to an empty directory: unbound `config.tracker_dir` follows it (the attack), but under the bound gate snapshot it resolves main's `.tickets-tracker`.\n- A remote with no fetched base fails closed: `gate_config` raises and `rebar verify-opcert` exits 2 naming `git fetch origin`.\n- A checkout with no remote reads its working tree.\n\nExisting `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py` and `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py` (remote-less fixtures) pass unchanged. Full `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The CI op-cert gate reads `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` from main's committed `rebar.toml`, not the change's: `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` fetches `origin/main` before `rebar verify-opcert`, and `gate_config` reads the project layer at that ref (`test_gate_config_ignores_the_working_tree_project_config`).\n- [ ] A change that adds a key to `rebar.toml` does not widen the trust list its own gate run uses: `test_change_adding_its_own_key_does_not_widen_its_gate_run` passes, and fails against the pre-fix `verify_opcert.py`.\n- [ ] A change setting `[tracker] dir` cannot redirect the store the gate walks: `test_change_cannot_redirect_the_store_it_walks` passes.\n- [ ] No config key, env var or flag is added: `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 and `git diff origin/main -- src/rebar/_config_schema.py` is empty.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py` passes."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795231811366427001,"uuid":"613a928b-5a4c-45a0-8316-d35557f8fa2c"}